      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=5fca89892730d8007611d907",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": {
      "content": [
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "I agree that it's not a clear-cut case, but it's the one we're inheriting from Apache.  I guess we could try to work around it... I'm not sure what that would look like. The POST behavior just takes the first part... Hmm. Well, i any case, worth re-opening if nothing else as a landmark to a muddled part of the API. ",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       }
      ],
      "type": "doc",
