  "comment": {
   "comments": [
    {
     "author": {
      "accountId": "5fca89892730d8007611d907",
      "accountType": "atlassian",
      "active": true,
      "avatarUrls": {
       "16x16": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/bf2e136284e0b17b99502dc3a32eef38?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FBA-6.png",
       "24x24": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/bf2e136284e0b17b99502dc3a32eef38?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FBA-6.png",
       "32x32": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/bf2e136284e0b17b99502dc3a32eef38?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FBA-6.png",
       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/bf2e136284e0b17b99502dc3a32eef38?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FBA-6.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Benjamin Armintor",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=5fca89892730d8007611d907",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": "<p>It is apparently believed that the semantics of PUT are incompatible with multipart request bodies, so I doubt that commons-fileupload regards this as a bug (and Fedora 3 is not going to change this dependency in the foreseeable future). See also <a href=\"http://www.w3.org/Protocols/rfc2616/rfc2616-sec9.html#sec9.6\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://www.w3.org/Protocols/rfc2616/rfc2616-sec9.html#sec9.6</a></p>",
     "created": "24/Jan/14 10:50 PM",
     "id": "12583",
     "jsdPublic": true,
     "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/11170/comment/12583",
     "updateAuthor": {
      "accountId": "5fca89892730d8007611d907",
      "accountType": "atlassian",
      "active": true,
      "avatarUrls": {
       "16x16": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/bf2e136284e0b17b99502dc3a32eef38?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FBA-6.png",
       "24x24": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/bf2e136284e0b17b99502dc3a32eef38?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FBA-6.png",
       "32x32": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/bf2e136284e0b17b99502dc3a32eef38?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FBA-6.png",
       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/bf2e136284e0b17b99502dc3a32eef38?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FBA-6.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Benjamin Armintor",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=5fca89892730d8007611d907",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "updated": "24/Jan/14 10:50 PM"
    },
    {
     "author": {
      "accountId": "557058:fb2ff2e4-636b-42c9-89c0-f91bd3f8435c",
      "accountType": "atlassian",
      "active": true,
      "avatarUrls": {
       "16x16": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/2b40121791d6946b6cdd805dc2ea4b7c?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FDB-3.png",
       "24x24": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/2b40121791d6946b6cdd805dc2ea4b7c?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FDB-3.png",
       "32x32": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/2b40121791d6946b6cdd805dc2ea4b7c?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FDB-3.png",
       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/2b40121791d6946b6cdd805dc2ea4b7c?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FDB-3.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Don Brower",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=557058%3Afb2ff2e4-636b-42c9-89c0-f91bd3f8435c",
      "timeZone": "America/New_York"
     },
     "body": "<p>Thanks for the answer. I don't completely follow how that section of RFC-2616 precludes multi-part uploads (e.g. what if all the files form a single semantic unit), but that is fine.</p>\n\n<p>FYI, the docs for modifyDatastream say the content should be multipart encoded.</p>\n\n<p><a href=\"https://wiki.duraspace.org/display/FEDORA37/REST+API#RESTAPI-modifyDatastream\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://wiki.duraspace.org/display/FEDORA37/REST+API#RESTAPI-modifyDatastream</a></p>",
     "created": "24/Jan/14 11:04 PM",
     "id": "12584",
     "jsdPublic": true,
     "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/11170/comment/12584",
     "updateAuthor": {
      "accountId": "557058:fb2ff2e4-636b-42c9-89c0-f91bd3f8435c",
      "accountType": "atlassian",
      "active": true,
      "avatarUrls": {
       "16x16": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/2b40121791d6946b6cdd805dc2ea4b7c?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FDB-3.png",
       "24x24": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/2b40121791d6946b6cdd805dc2ea4b7c?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FDB-3.png",
       "32x32": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/2b40121791d6946b6cdd805dc2ea4b7c?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FDB-3.png",
       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/2b40121791d6946b6cdd805dc2ea4b7c?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FDB-3.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Don Brower",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=557058%3Afb2ff2e4-636b-42c9-89c0-f91bd3f8435c",
      "timeZone": "America/New_York"
     },
     "updated": "24/Jan/14 11:04 PM"
    },
    {
     "author": {
      "accountId": "5fca89892730d8007611d907",
      "accountType": "atlassian",
      "active": true,
      "avatarUrls": {
       "16x16": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/bf2e136284e0b17b99502dc3a32eef38?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FBA-6.png",
       "24x24": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/bf2e136284e0b17b99502dc3a32eef38?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FBA-6.png",
       "32x32": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/bf2e136284e0b17b99502dc3a32eef38?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FBA-6.png",
       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/bf2e136284e0b17b99502dc3a32eef38?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FBA-6.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Benjamin Armintor",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=5fca89892730d8007611d907",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": "<p>I agree that it's not a clear-cut case, but it's the one we're inheriting from Apache.  I guess we could try to work around it... I'm not sure what that would look like. The POST behavior just takes the first part... Hmm. Well, i any case, worth re-opening if nothing else as a landmark to a muddled part of the API. </p>",
     "created": "24/Jan/14 11:35 PM",
     "id": "12585",
     "jsdPublic": true,
     "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/11170/comment/12585",
