  "description": "<p>Trying to update a datastream using a multipart encoded PUT request does not work. Fedora will save the multipart wrapper in the datastream contents. See attached file for example.</p>\n\n<p>It seems like the problem is here:</p>\n\n<p><a href=\"https://github.com/fcrepo/fcrepo/blob/master/fcrepo-server/src/main/java/org/fcrepo/server/rest/RestUtil.java#L45\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://github.com/fcrepo/fcrepo/blob/master/fcrepo-server/src/main/java/org/fcrepo/server/rest/RestUtil.java#L45</a></p>\n\n<p>because isMultipartContent() only recognizes multipart messages that use the POST method:</p>\n\n<p><a href=\"http://commons.apache.org/proper/commons-fileupload/apidocs/src-html/org/apache/commons/fileupload/servlet/ServletFileUpload.html#line.66\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://commons.apache.org/proper/commons-fileupload/apidocs/src-html/org/apache/commons/fileupload/servlet/ServletFileUpload.html#line.66</a></p>",
